From ab69f08715d70c6ac5feac7afd543d5761ce4e7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:21:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wait for a week of evidence before scoring anyone
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

₹2,000 of pocket money with ₹1,500 already spent was reading as perfect
health. Not a scoring bug — the detectors were behaving correctly. Every
one of them compares this week against a normal, one day of history has
no normal in it, so they all found nothing and reported nothing wrong.
Absence of evidence rendered as evidence of absence, in green, at 100
out of 100.

So nothing gets a number until there is a week of spending AND at least
three payments. Either alone can be met without evidence: seven days can
be one backdated entry, three payments can all be from this morning.
A week is also the shortest span where "unusual" means anything, because
spending is weekly — a baseline that has not seen a weekend calls every
Saturday a surge.

Until then Home shows how far off it is (3/7, with a bar) instead of a
score, and the Future tab says the same rather than announcing a 100%
chance of running out on a named date off a single observation. A
confident date built on one data point is a guess wearing a decimal
point, and the reader cannot tell the difference. Importing a bank
statement clears the gate in one go, which is the intended way in.

Also in here, both from testing on the phone:

- Onboarding and Try It still asked for dates as typed YYYY-MM-DD text
  while every other date field had a calendar. Now they have it too, and
  Try It's window is enforced by the picker rather than explained in
  grey text underneath.
- The Home empty state was a card telling you to go to the Spending tab.
  Telling someone where to tap, on a screen you could have made
  tappable, is a dead end with instructions written on it. It is a
  button now, and it lands on the add form with the sheet already open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017qsfq3JXWhwEdcaLUroXZy
